stagefright: Build the codec list without an OMX store

The Echo Dot (2nd gen) leaves out the OMX service. OmxInfoBuilder then
failed with NO_INIT, MediaCodecList dropped every codec with it, the
Codec2 software codecs included, and MediaCodecList.getCodecCount()
crashed apps in JNI. Without a store there are just no OMX codecs.

diff --git a/media/libstagefright/OmxInfoBuilder.cpp b/media/libstagefright/OmxInfoBuilder.cpp
index 79ffdeb..e622c12 100644
--- a/media/libstagefright/OmxInfoBuilder.cpp
+++ b/media/libstagefright/OmxInfoBuilder.cpp
@@ -95,8 +95,11 @@ status_t OmxInfoBuilder::buildMediaCodecList(MediaCodecListWriter* writer) {
     // Obtain IOmxStore
     sp<IOmxStore> omxStore = IOmxStore::getService();
     if (omxStore == nullptr) {
-        ALOGE("Cannot find an IOmxStore service.");
-        return NO_INIT;
+        // A device without OMX codecs, like the Echo Dot (2nd gen), still
+        // has the Codec2 software ones. Failing here would leave no codec
+        // list at all.
+        ALOGI("No IOmxStore service, so no OMX codecs.");
+        return OK;
     }
 
     // List service attributes (global settings)
